---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<Base title="Cost & timeline" description="What a middleware migration typically costs and how long it takes, explained plainly.">
  <section class="section on-dark">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cost &amp; timeline</p>
      <h1>What does a middleware migration cost, and how long does it take?</h1>
      <p class="lead">You shouldn't have to sit through a sales cycle to get a sense of scale. Here are our typical figures, and what changes them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid grid-2">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Typical cost</p>
        <p class="stat">£3,000–£5,000</p>
        <p><strong>per interface, all-in.</strong> An interface is one connection between systems, for example orders flowing from your website into your finance system.</p>
        <p>The price covers discovery, analysis, infrastructure, build, automated testing, go-live and close support afterwards.</p>
        <p>Your actual figure depends on the source technology and the complexity of each interface. We present it after the assessment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Typical timeline</p>
        <p class="stat">6–12 months</p>
        <p>As a guide, around <strong>30 interfaces take about 6 months</strong> and <strong>100 interfaces take about 12 months</strong>.</p>
        <p>The pace is usually set by how quickly your organisation can accept change, not by how fast the migration can be built.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section tint">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <details>
        <summary>What makes an interface more or less expensive?</summary>
        <p>The source platform, the number of systems involved, the complexity of the mapping and business rules, and how much documentation already exists.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is the assessment really free?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Our AI-assisted assessment and sizing is free of charge. You get an inventory, a view of complexity and risk, and an indicative cost and timeline.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can we migrate in phases?</summary>
        <p>Yes. Most migrations run in phases, so value arrives early and each go-live is small and controlled.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens after go-live?</summary>
        <p>Each phase includes close support until it is stable. Your team is left with integrations that are documented, tested and monitored.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand heading="Get a figure for your estate" />
</Base>
